        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Treadmills for Sale", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/treadmills-for-sale/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "When is the best time to buy a treadmill on sale?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The late-autumn promotional period and the model-year changeover are the two windows where discounts are real. January is the worst time — demand peaks, stock thins, and prices are often higher than they were six weeks earlier. The outgoing model year is usually the best value in the category, because annual refreshes are overwhelmingly console changes over unchanged hardware.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is it cheaper to buy a treadmill online or in a store?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Online is usually cheaper at checkout and a specialty dealer is often cheaper by the time the machine is running in your house. The dealer price typically includes delivery into the room and assembly, which online sellers charge $150-$300 for as an add-on, and you get to stand on the machine before committing.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are refurbished treadmills worth buying?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Frequently yes, at 15-30% below new — but the discount is not the variable that matters. Warranty term is. Factory-refurbished units range from a full original warranty to 90 days, listings often do not say which, and a refurbished machine with 90 days of cover is a materially different purchase from one with the full term.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much should I pay for a used treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "As a rough anchor, expect to pay 40-50% of current street price for a well-maintained machine three to five years old, and considerably less beyond that. Only pay anything at all for a machine you have run under power and walked on at two speeds. Budget for a lubrication and belt tension check on arrival regardless of what the seller says.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What does delivery of a treadmill actually involve?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
