            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Technically usually, practically rarely. Restocking fees, freight return shipping and a requirement to re-crate the machine can add up to a third of the purchase price. That asymmetry is the reason a forgiving return policy is worth more than a small discount, and the reason trying a machine in person is still the best risk control available.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Morgan Reyes" },
      datePublished: "2026-09-15",
