        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Decide the specification before you look at a single price. Deck length, continuous-duty
            rating and weight capacity are what you are buying; everything else on the listing is
            how it is being sold to you.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then buy the outgoing model year from a seller whose returns and delivery you have
            actually read. The best prices in this category come from
            <a href="/best-time-of-year-to-buy-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">timing the changeover</a>
            or from the <a href="/new-vs-used-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">used market</a>
            — not from the banner at the top of a product page.
          </p>
